---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const indexEvidenceResult = await indexEvidence(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const mapCompetenciesResult = await mapCompetencies(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, indexEvidenceResult.accepted);
const assessSufficiencyResult = await assessSufficiency(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, mapCompetenciesResult.accepted);
const formNextTasksResult = await formNextTasks(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, assessSufficiencyResult.accepted);
const prepareAssessmentResult = await prepareAssessment(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, formNextTasksResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { indexEvidence: indexEvidenceResult, mapCompetencies: mapCompetenciesResult, assessSufficiency: assessSufficiencyResult, formNextTasks: formNextTasksResult, prepareAssessment: prepareAssessmentResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...indexEvidenceResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...mapCompetenciesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...assessSufficiencyResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...formNextTasksResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...prepareAssessmentResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...indexEvidenceResult.checks, ...mapCompetenciesResult.checks, ...assessSufficiencyResult.checks, ...formNextTasksResult.checks, ...prepareAssessmentResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A group project lacks contribution records: request an individual demonstration rather than assuming equal authorship. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (request an individual demonstration rather than assuming equal authorship.) through the existing stage result for PortfolioEvidence; preserve exact source/version and the prior PortfolioEvidence, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — Evidence is old but relevant: apply the supplied recency rule rather than an invented cutoff. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (apply the supplied recency rule rather than an invented cutoff.) through the existing stage result for PortfolioEvidence; preserve exact source/version and the prior PortfolioEvidence, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A supervisor comment conflicts with the artifact: preserve both and request clarification. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (preserve both and request clarification.) through the existing stage result for PortfolioEvidence; preserve exact source/version and the prior PortfolioEvidence, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — An accommodation changes the form of evidence: assess the same competency through an approved alternative. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (assess the same competency through an approved alternative.) through the existing stage result for PortfolioEvidence; preserve exact source/version and the prior PortfolioEvidence, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A learner appeals an attribution error: version the finding and reassess affected competencies. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (version the finding and reassess affected competencies.) through the existing stage result for PortfolioEvidence; preserve exact source/version and the prior PortfolioEvidence, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, indexEvidence: indexEvidenceResult, mapCompetencies: mapCompetenciesResult, assessSufficiency: assessSufficiencyResult, formNextTasks: formNextTasksResult, prepareAssessment: prepareAssessmentResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
